# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# The server binary, from a plain `go build` in the repository or its directory
/garmin-mcp
/cmd/garmin-mcp/garmin-mcp

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
!coverage.go
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# The Go workspace (go.work) is committed: it builds the server against the
# library in this repository. See "For developers" in README.md.

# env file
.env
key
token
# Editor/IDE
# .idea/
# .vscode/

# Raw live API responses (personal data: GPS, heart rate). Never commit.
**/testdata/live/

# Deployment secrets
deploy/secrets/
deploy/.env

# Secrets for `fly secrets import`
fly-secrets.env

# Fly app config: names the personal app, so each deployer writes their own (docs/fly.md)
fly.toml
fly.toml.orig

# IDE settings (personal)
.idea/
